Hold a 1024-byte block, and drop truncated datagrams

libnyoci sizes its one receive buffer, which DTLS records also pass
through, as NYOCI_MAX_CONTENT_LENGTH + 8 = 1032 bytes. That is below
RFC 7252 Section 4.6's 1152-byte message size. A peer sending a
1024-byte Block1 block, which is libcoap's and cantcoap's default, has
its datagram cut short. recvmsg() was not asked about MSG_TRUNC, so
the cut message was processed as if whole: plain CoAP reassembled the
wrong bytes and answered 4.08, and DTLS failed to decrypt and timed
out.

Raise the default content length to 1280. That holds a 1024-byte block
plus its options and, with DTLS record overhead, still fits a 1500-byte
Ethernet MTU. A datagram larger even than that is now dropped as lost,
not processed truncated.

The default lives in an installed header (nyoci-defaults.h), so
libnyoci and its consumers agree on the size of every struct that
embeds a packet buffer.

diff --git a/src/libnyoci/nyoci-defaults.h b/src/libnyoci/nyoci-defaults.h
index 91c6ef7..fb0c66a 100644
--- a/src/libnyoci/nyoci-defaults.h
+++ b/src/libnyoci/nyoci-defaults.h
@@ -82,7 +82,11 @@
 #if NYOCI_USE_UIP
 #define NYOCI_MAX_PACKET_LENGTH ((UIP_BUFSIZE - UIP_LLH_LEN - UIP_IPUDPH_LEN))
 #else
-#define NYOCI_MAX_CONTENT_LENGTH     (1024)
+// Kythira: 1024 made the receive buffer 1032 bytes, below RFC 7252
+// Section 4.6's 1152-byte message size, so a peer's 1024-byte Block1 block
+// arrived truncated. 1280 holds a 1024-byte block plus its options, and
+// with DTLS record overhead still fits a 1500-byte Ethernet MTU.
+#define NYOCI_MAX_CONTENT_LENGTH     (1280)
 #endif
 #endif
 
diff --git a/src/plat-net/posix/nyoci-plat-net.c b/src/plat-net/posix/nyoci-plat-net.c
index d9174a3..bae25ae 100644
--- a/src/plat-net/posix/nyoci-plat-net.c
+++ b/src/plat-net/posix/nyoci-plat-net.c
@@ -884,6 +884,12 @@ nyoci_plat_process(
 
 				require_action(packet_len > 0, bail, ret = NYOCI_STATUS_ERRNO);
 
+				// Kythira: a datagram larger than the buffer used to be
+				// processed cut short. Drop it instead, as a lost packet.
+				if (msg.msg_flags & MSG_TRUNC) {
+					continue;
+				}
+
 				packet[packet_len] = 0;
 
